ments in the Middle East. These factors are highly interrelated and are not separately quantified by us in a manner that permits us to determine with reasonable precision the individual impact of each factor. Inside merchandise sales increased due to $7.4 million, or 74.0%, of incremental sales from new stores and $2.8 million attributable to a 28.0% increase in same-store sales, partially offset by $0.2 million decrease due to closed stores.","context":"Revenue","section":"Factors Affecting the Comparability of Our Results of Operations","block":638,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-095497","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001859836","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1859836/000110465926095497/tmb-20260630x10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/239f759192cdf63e873742b634fbac5aedc90412fe8dd8b5512cc65b13acfff1.bin","sha256":"239f759192cdf63e873742b634fbac5aedc90412fe8dd8b5512cc65b13acfff1"}},{"id":"e741e939aa9d678d5bb0a86579b044722c43b1758b3c94925f0d8ddfdd50b5d0","quote":"Cost of Goods Sold (exclusive of depreciation and amortization)","context":"Expenses","section":"Factors Affecting the Comparability of Our Results of Operations","block":640,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-095497","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001859836","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1859836/000110465926095497/tmb-20260630x10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/239f759192cdf63e873742b634fbac5aedc90412fe8dd8b5512cc65b13acfff1.bin","sha256":"239f759192cdf63e873742b634fbac5aedc90412fe8dd8b5512cc65b13acfff1"}},{"id":"5378a2f6198602cf41fdedcc6eb0fe801ef19bf67674dd7fc77eef3a737f3ac9","quote":"Cost of goods sold (exclusive of depreciation and amortization) was $743.5 million for the three months ended June 30, 2026, an increase of $215.4 million, or 40.8%, compared to the three months ended June 30, 2025. This increase was attributable to $210.1 million increase of higher fuel cost of goods sold (exclusive of depreciation and amortization) and $5.3 million of higher inside merchandise cost of goods sold (exclusive of depreciation and amortization), primarily resulting from the related increase in sales. The increase in fuel cost of goods sold (exclusive of depreciation and amortization) was driven by a $26.2 million increase associated with higher fuel gallons sold and $183.9 million increase resulting from a 45.4% increase in the average per-gallon cost of fuel. The increase in average per gallon cost of fuel primarily reflects changes in market supply and demand dynamics, wholesale fuel price levels, and volatility, which were influenced by recent geopolitical developments in the Middle East.","context":"Cost of Goods Sold (exclusive of depreciation and amortization)","section":"Factors Affecting the Comparability of Our Results of Operations","block":641,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-095497","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001859836","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1859836/000110465926095497/tmb-20260630x10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/239f759192cdf63e873742b634fbac5aedc90412fe8dd8b5512cc65b13acfff1.bin","sha256":"239f759192cdf63e873742b634fbac5aedc90412fe8dd8b5512cc65b13acfff1"}},{"id":"a412720eb87f90f02fee63c2e63392b36394133ce9d4e2db2edcad8be0591955","quote":"Salaries and employee benefits increased by $5.6 million, or 11.2%, for the three months ended June 30, 2026, compared to the three months ended June 30, 2025. Of this increase, approximately $4.7 million was related to equity-based compensation and approximately $1.3 million was related to new stores, partially offset by approximately $0.6 million decrease in same store costs due to better labor scheduling and approximately $0.1 million related to closed stores. Equity-based compensation only reflects a partial period due to the grants having been issued in conjunction with the IPO. In future periods, equity-based compensation is expected to increase as a result of recognition over a full period.","context":"Salaries and Employee Benefits","section":"Factors Affecting the Comparability of Our Results of Operations","block":643,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-095497","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001859836","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1859836/000110465926095497/tmb-20260630x10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/239f759192cdf63e873742b634fbac5aedc90412fe8dd8b5512cc65b13acfff1.bin","sha256":"239f759192cdf63e873742b634fbac5aedc90412fe8dd8b5512cc65b13acfff1"}},{"id":"3e3a3d949eefed441e885dcdef1a79500eb3fe9a22927be930e45b35bc362113","quote":"Selling, General, and Administrative Expenses","context":"Salaries and employee benefits increased by $5.6 million, or 11.2%, for the three months ended June 30, 2026, compared to the three months ended June 30, 2025. Of this increase, approximately $4.7 million was related to equity-based compensation and approximately $1.3 million was related to new stores, partially offset by approximately $0.6 million decrease in same store costs due to better labor scheduling and approximately $0.1 million related to closed stores. Equity-based compensation only reflects a partial period due to the grants having been issued in conjunction with the IPO. In future periods, equity-based compensation is expected to increase as a result of recognition over a full period.","section":"Factors Affecting the Comparability of Our Results of Operations","block":644,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-095497","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001859836","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1859836/000110465926095497/tmb-20260630x10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/239f759192cdf63e873742b634fbac5aedc90412fe8dd8b5512cc65b13acfff1.bin","sha256":"239f759192cdf63e873742b634fbac5aedc90412fe8dd8b5512cc65b13acfff1"}},{"id":"d055323c5c8902a7c5d812d667ff1be8dd5beb73b962d000f992b6610ccc0120","quote":"Selling, general, and administrative expenses increased by $8.3 million, or 17.1%, for the three months ended June 30, 2026, compared to the three months ended June 30, 2025. This increase was primarily driven by an increase in charge card fees of $4.6 million related to the increase in sales, $1.0 million increase in insurance expense due to development on certain claims, and $1.9 million increase in facility expenses for new build-to-suit activity, partially offset by a $0.4 million decrease for IPO related costs incurred and acquisition expenses compared to the three months ended June 30, 2025.","context":"Selling, General, and Administrative Expenses","section":"Factors Affecting the Comparability of Our Results of Operations","block":645,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-095497","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001859836","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1859836/000110465926095497/tmb-20260630x10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/239f759192cdf63e873742b634fbac5aedc90412fe8dd8b5512cc65b13acfff1.bin","sha256":"239f759192cdf63e873742b634fbac5aedc90412fe8dd8b5512cc65b13acfff1"}},{"id":"1114f6a4b1d25384243cc862a1cd1cdcbb9a3d7fe7cbeef09f950f1a702a41c2","quote":"Depreciation, amortization, and accretion expense increased by $0.9 million, or 5.9%, for the three months ended June 30, 2026, compared to the three months ended June 30, 2025. This increase was due primarily to capital expenditures for new stores.","context":"Depreciation, Amortization, and Accretion","section":"Factors Affecting the Comparability of Our Results of Operations","block":647,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-095497","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001859836","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1859836/000110465926095497/tmb-20260630x10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/239f759192cdf63e873742b634fbac5aedc90412fe8dd8b5512cc65b13acfff1.bin","sha256":"239f759192cdf63e873742b634fbac5aedc90412fe8dd8b5512cc65b13acfff1"}},{"id":"495088e6912b6c0b7a071ca43c8999b6816582d4ca4cef0bb8e7075cea7c6e13","quote":"Gain on disposal of assets decreased by $2.0 million for the three months ended June 30, 2026, compared to the three months ended June 30, 2025. This decrease was due primarily to sales of miscellaneous real estate assets.","context":"Loss (Gain) on Disposal of Assets","section":"Factors Affecting the Comparability of Our Results of Operations","block":651,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-095497","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001859836","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1859836/000110465926095497/tmb-20260630x10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/239f759192cdf63e873742b634fbac5aedc90412fe8dd8b5512cc65b13acfff1.bin","sha256":"239f759192cdf63e873742b634fbac5aedc90412fe8dd8b5512cc65b13acfff1"}},{"id":"eaf5773cdc59ba6dd8b395c939212745ba8973c9486defd587823ddf8bf28f7f","quote":"Interest expense, net decreased by $2.6 million for the three months ended June 30, 2026, compared to the three months ended June 30, 2025. The decrease in interest expense, net was primarily due to a reduction in our outstanding borrowings under our Revolving Credit Facility and a reduction in 